  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Produced on the occasion of an exhibition that was shown at the Binghamton University Art Museum from Sept. 28 through Nov. 3, 2007, organized by Lynn Gamwell, director of the Museum.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Presents thirty artworks, each consisting of an original photograph presented alongside a page from the Encyclopædia Britannica (ca. 1950-1970) that the artist has scanned and reprinted. The artwork consists of this combination, and it is the artist's intention that neither element be exhibited without the other."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="504" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Includes bibliographical references.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="505" ind1="2" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Trick of the I : observation and invention in Jeff Gibson's Sarsaparilla to Sorcery / Jeffrey Kastner.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Australian-born artist Jeff Gibson pairs open-ended, abstract photographic images with pages torn from encyclopedias from the 1950s, 60s and 70s.</subfield>
  </datafield>
